          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            In as far as the notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            generalizes that of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
            and that of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/profunctor"} profunctor
            generalizes that of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relation"} relation
            %em graph
            of a (pro)functor generalizes that of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graph+of+a+function"} graph of a function
          %p
            Just as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graph+of+a+function"} graph of a function
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : X \to Y
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relation"} relation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mi X
                  %mo ×
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R \subset X \times Y
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Y
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi Set
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                  %mi Cat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X,Y \in Set = 0 Cat
            is nothing but the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+elements"} category of elements
            of the corresponding characteristic function
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi χ
                      %mi R
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi Y
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi Cat
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi_R : X \times Y \to (-1)Cat = \{0,1\}
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F\colon C \to D
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/profunctor"} profunctor
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                    %mo :
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi op
                    %mo ×
                    %mi D
                    %mo →
                    %mn 0
                    %mi Cat
                    %mo =
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H : C^{op} \times D \to 0 Cat = Set
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+elements"} category of elements
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+construction"} Grothendieck construction
          %p
            However, there are a number of different ways to construct such a category of elements, depending on the variance of morphisms in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            that we include in it. A one-variable functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C\to Set
            has two categories of elements, one with a projection to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            (which is a
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+opfibration"} discrete opfibration
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^{op}
            (which is a
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+fibration"} discrete fibration
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi op
                  %mo ×
                  %mi D
                  %mo →
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H : C^{op}\times D\to Set
            has
            %em four
            categories of elements; thus a profunctor has four different “graphs”. In addition, there are two ways to make a functor into a profunctor, so a functor actually has
            %em eight
            graphs.
          %h2#definition Definition
          %h3#graphs_of_a_profunctor Graphs of a profunctor
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi op
                  %mo ×
                  %mi D
                  %mo →
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H:C^{op} \times D \to Set
            be a
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/profunctor"} profunctor
            = succeed "." do
              %strong graphs
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi c
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi C
                    %mo ,
                    %mi d
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi D
                    %mo ,
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi c
                    %mo ,
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (c\in C, d\in D, x\in H(c,d))
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi c
                  %mo ,
                  %mi d
                  %mo ,
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi c
                  %mo ′
                  %mo ,
                  %mi d
                  %mo ′
                  %mo ,
                  %mi x
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (c,d,x) \to (c',d',x')
            to be any of the following:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Pairs
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi f
                      %mo :
                      %mi c
                      %mo →
                      %mi c
                      %mo ′
                      %mo ,
                      %mi g
                      %mo :
                      %mi d
                      %mo →
                      %mi d
                      %mo ′
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f:c\to c', g:d\to d')
                such that
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi H
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mi g
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mi H
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi f
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo ′
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H(1,g)(x) = H(f,1)(x')
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                        %mo ×
                        %mi D
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C\times D
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/two-sided+discrete+fibration"} two-sided discrete fibration
                that is contravariant over
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                and covariant over
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi D
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            %li
              %p
                Pairs
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi f
                      %mo :
                      %mi c
                      %mo ′
                      %mo →
                      %mi c
                      %mo ,
                      %mi g
                      %mo :
                      %mi d
                      %mo →
                      %mi d
                      %mo ′
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f:c'\to c, g:d\to d')
                such that
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi H
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi f
                        %mo ,
                        %mi g
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mi x
                        %mo ′
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H(f,g)(x) = x'
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi C
                          %mi op
                        %mo ×
                        %mi D
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^{op}\times D
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+opfibration"} discrete opfibration
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comma+category"} comma category
                = succeed ":" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mi H
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (*\downarrow H)
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi Graph
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi H
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mtd
                              %mo →
                            %mtd
                              %mo *
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mtd
                              %mo ⇙
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mi C
                                %mi op
                              %mo ×
                              %mi D
                            %mtd
                              %mover
                                %mo →
                                %mi H
                            %mtd
                              %mi Set
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\array{
                      Graph(H) &amp;\to&amp; {*}
                      \\\
                      \\downarrow &amp; \swArrow &amp; \downarrow
                      \\\
                      C^{op} \times D &amp;\stackrel{H}{\to}&amp; Set
                      }
            %li
              %p
                Pairs
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi f
                      %mo :
                      %mi c
                      %mo →
                      %mi c
                      %mo ′
                      %mo ,
                      %mi g
                      %mo :
                      %mi d
                      %mo ′
                      %mo →
                      %mi d
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f:c\to c', g:d'\to d)
                such that
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi H
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi f
                        %mo ,
                        %mi g
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo ′
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mi x
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H(f,g)(x') = x
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                        %mo ×
                        %msup
                          %mi D
                          %mi op
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C\times D^{op}
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+fibration"} discrete fibration
            %li
              %p
                Pairs
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi f
                      %mo :
                      %mi c
                      %mo ′
                      %mo →
                      %mi c
                      %mo ,
                      %mi g
                      %mo :
                      %mi d
                      %mo ′
                      %mo →
                      %mi d
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f:c'\to c, g:d'\to d)
                such that
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi H
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mi g
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo ′
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mi H
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi f
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H(1,g)(x') = H(f,1)(x)
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi C
                          %mi op
                        %mo ×
                        %msup
                          %mi D
                          %mi op
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^{op}\times D^{op}
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/two-sided+discrete+fibration"} two-sided discrete fibration
                that is covariant over
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mi op
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^{op}
                and contravariant over
                = succeed ";" do
